      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceCors_1a8bdb2553f14222ee4cacfb5628907590" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void Cors::apply</definition>
        <argsstring>(const drogon::HttpRequestPtr &amp;req, const drogon::HttpResponsePtr &amp;resp)</argsstring>
        <name>apply</name>
        <qualifiedname>Cors::apply</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const drogon::HttpRequestPtr &amp;</type>
          <declname>req</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const drogon::HttpResponsePtr &amp;</type>
          <declname>resp</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Decorates a response with CORS headers; invoked once per response from the pre-sending advice. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If the response already carries Access-Control-Allow-Origin: &quot;*&quot;, it is left untouched. Otherwise the current cors_allowed_origins setting is read from the Configurator. An exact match to the request&apos;s Origin is reflected back with Allow-Credentials and Vary: Origin; if origins are configured but none match, the first configured origin is used without credentials; if the setting is &quot;*&quot;, the wildcard is used. For OPTIONS requests a sanitized echo of Access-Control-Request-Headers replaces the default header list, and Max-Age plus Vary are added. Every write uses HttpResponse::addHeader, which replaces an existing value rather than duplicating it. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">req</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Request being answered; supplies Origin and, for preflights, the requested headers. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">resp</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Response to decorate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>No shared mutable state is modified here; the configuration is read through <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>&apos;s thread-local cache. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="namespaceCorsTokens_1ab923849059179cf6c8fb446aa5cb5e5d" kindref="member">CorsTokens::sanitizeRequestedHeaders()</ref>, <ref refid="namespaceCorsTokens_1a0868524c04d18e34760e18676a1ff72f" kindref="member">CorsTokens::mergeVary()</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
